{"id": "EUVD-2026-86783", "enisaUuid": "a02b5b54-4cdb-3923-9366-90bbb79cae10", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: usbusx2y: validate URB actual_length in interrupt callback\n\ni_usx2y_in04_int() processes the interrupt URB data without checking\nurb->actual_length.  A short transfer from a malfunctioning device\nwould cause the handler to process uninitialized heap data from the\nkmalloc-allocated in04_buf, which is then copied to the mmap-accessible\nctl_snapshot[] array.\n\nFix by using kzalloc() for in04_buf to zero-initialize the buffer,\nand adding an actual_length check to skip processing on short\ntransfers while still resubmitting the URB.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3576cb77b527f223cf2b9fc2b2e9af5e7adee25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c156584999bf15118f523ef6c6fedc5b21f46bd9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0c30fe6c0d5902bd8a7d1d5720bead5bbe46f7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2770321b358658e0a39fe39ccf6a91ee97a81931", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f5ef203abda9dd36b2af473c7b737d544f807bd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97929", "GHSA-7jc2-x3x6-f88w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d73d8dd-0f32-34db-a58c-77d1f453d9db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "212f284d-b833-3701-a4b0-d86f04bc1c89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "301f2bb1-6a9d-3e72-b341-5edc49f87a36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "547c9c83-ca44-38e4-8a02-fcdaa1a51b24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <8f5ef203abda9dd36b2af473c7b737d544f807bd"}, {"id": "73c6bc21-9616-32b2-bec7-1c21c71bc5ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8e7b4a7f-08c3-31e2-acc7-cdf6f36f6ceb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "964c1a2c-b79d-3cbd-b772-5bbb9667b514", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b0c30fe6c0d5902bd8a7d1d5720bead5bbe46f7d"}, {"id": "a1f58119-cf0e-38d2-9b10-46bbe7c733ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c156584999bf15118f523ef6c6fedc5b21f46bd9"}, {"id": "d5fcb92a-db51-3e96-bbc5-10708472b444", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e07c5b1d-00eb-33f9-ac8e-c5e310f765ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "e3445002-5863-31d1-b022-5ac55f318fe3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2770321b358658e0a39fe39ccf6a91ee97a81931"}, {"id": "e6dece4d-c967-3e64-89f4-158a974fdfed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c3576cb77b527f223cf2b9fc2b2e9af5e7adee25"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6658b12f-f0c4-3e6c-83c4-d3eb8a33de0f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}